  document.getElementById('count').textContent = '4 of 4 results';
  event.currentTarget.remove();
});
```

So upon click, it adds two items, updates count, and removes the button (#more) from DOM via `event.currentTarget.remove()`.

Now, focusing: When a button is removed, if it currently has focus, focus may shift elsewhere (maybe to body). After removal, focus lost, thus #results:focus-within becomes false.

